# failed_bindings uses Type::Error — no E099 cascade
# When a dict entry fails type checking, downstream references should
# propagate Type::Error (not cascade into E099 runtime crashes).
# After B-282: [+ 1 "string"] is caught statically (Addable Int String has
# no instance), so x gets Type::Error. The eval still produces E013 at runtime
# because the evaluator always runs regardless of type errors.

[x: [+ 1 "string"]]
[y: x]
y
=== error
[E013] no instance for Addable (Int, String) (defined at 7:5-7:19)
  in [+ ...] at 7:5-7:19
